# One person, three author strings, 58 commits.
#
# The history carries `thedamon-wizard <amon.koike@daemons.jp>` (27 commits, a typo for the
# GitHub handle), `a-koike <amon06251994@gmail.com>` (22) and `Amon Koike
# <amon.koike@daemons.jp>` (10).  This submission states a sole author, so a reviewer running
# `git shortlog -sne` on the public repository would otherwise see three contributors and have
# to guess whether that contradicts the claim.
#
# Mapping is by commit email, which collapses both daemons.jp name variants and the gmail
# address without rewriting a single commit.  History is evidence; a canonical-name file is the
# supported way to correct how it reads.
